{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17163 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "Norarecoline is implicated in the pathogenesis of HaCaT cells through a series of mechanistic links that converge on the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is a target of Norarecoline, and its inhibition is associated with the activation of downstream pathways that ultimately affect HaCaT cells. The evidence suggests that Norarecoline exerts its effects by targeting this enzyme, which in turn influences the activity of other compounds, such as 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, both of which have a target of HaCaT. These findings collectively indicate that Norarecoline may modulate cellular processes in HaCaT cells through the inhibition of a key metabolic enzyme, potentially leading to a therapeutic effect. The consistent targeting of SDR family member 9 across different compounds supports a unified mechanism of action, suggesting that Norarecoline's interaction with HaCaT cells is mediated through this enzyme.",
